comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-22T18:24:13.924Z",codex-root,"Duplicate check: all-status searches for roadmap horizon, portfolio sequencing, now-next-later, exploratory planning, and promotion policy found the living milestone pm-doxj and initiative-specific notes but no decision governing evidence-based movement across the portfolio. This item defines governance only; it does not duplicate any delivery feature, epic, or prior point-in-time review."
  "2026-07-22T18:26:36.084Z",codex-root,"Baseline evidence: root help currently exposes 75 top-level names while contracts summary exposes 63 compact command summaries. The established pm-n7rr partition already assigns every spelling to a canonical noun family, hidden alias, internal helper, extension-owned surface, or generated discovery path. Promotion policy therefore treats simplification as delivery against existing canonical items, never as feature removal or a fresh command taxonomy."
  "2026-07-22T18:28:18.329Z",codex-root,"Verification evidence 2026-07-22: post-organization tracker totals are 1,914 items, 1,922 history streams, and 32,188 events before this evidence comment. Validate is ok with zero history drift; the known terminal-resolution warning remains 277 items under pm-e9zh and the five historical unknown-author events remain under pm-h90s. Graph audit reports 1,917 nodes and 3,366 edges, 223 active nodes, zero active isolates, zero active degree-one nodes, and only the same informational terminal legacy findings. Exact/fuzzy duplicate results remain the known canceled probe cluster and parent-scope duplicate count is zero. All active non-root items have acceptance criteria, estimates, tags, and parents. pnpm build, changelog verification, contracts verification, and the full static quality gate passed, including package boundary and token-budget gates."
  "2026-07-22T18:29:11.957Z",codex-root,"Publication evidence: substantive tracker organization commit 068b1e3d013c15eb23d952c484be075700fc65a6 was pushed directly to origin/main as explicitly requested, without a PR or review workflow. GitHub reported the expected required-status-check bypass for the direct push. Exact local HEAD and origin/main matched after fetch. gh run list for that commit returned no workflow runs, consistent with tracker-only path filtering; local build, changelog, contracts, static-quality, package-boundary, token-budget, tracker validation, graph, and duplicate checks are recorded above."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-22T18:24:13.924Z",codex-root,"Initial horizon model: Current = command grammar, SDK boundary completion, active graph/context/governance foundations; Emerging = derived index, evaluation, memory tiers, million-item and concurrency proof; Expansion = universal SDK exemplars, cross-workspace federation, signatures, role policy, event coordination; Exploratory = temporal digital twins and accepted cognitive-context subsystems. Quality, security, documentation, immutable proof, and token budgets are continuous constraints rather than a separate terminal phase."
  "2026-07-26T06:04:15.955Z","harness:claude-code","Long-horizon planning pass 2026-07-26. This note argues for one addition to the horizon policy: the six outcome milestones under pm-doxj are a complete ladder for reaching v1.0 and the universal-platform claim, and they are all bounded by things this project controls. Nothing in the portfolio is horizoned against things it does not control, and for a tool whose stated target is workspaces spanning several decades, that is the gap worth naming before another milestone is ever considered.\n\nWhere the ladder currently ends. j82fd3 (grammar), 9rgaal (SDK-complete), w7ccmv (provable history), o87av6 (proven scale), xp1xsw (v1.0 GA), t4d7nz (universal domain platform). Each is falsifiable, each has an owner, and after the 2026-07-26 edge pass each is reachable from 268 of 271 active items through typed implements and verifies paths. The ladder is not missing a rung. What it is missing is a statement of what happens after the last rung, on a timescale where the assumptions underneath every rung stop holding.\n\nThree decade-scale forces, each with a concrete near-term consequence that can be acted on now rather than planned for later.\n\n1. The reader outlives the writer. pm-e5yupa already requires a declared support window per format version and a CI-proven reader for the oldest supported version. The decade-scale version of that requirement is stronger and cheaper to adopt now than later: the on-disk format should be readable by a program that has never seen this codebase. pm-4jk8kx (open workspace format specification with a conformance suite) is the item that makes that true, and its real justification is not interoperability with other tools today but readability by tools that do not exist yet. A workspace whose only reader is this binary is a workspace with a 5-to-10 year life, whatever the support policy says. Recommend promoting pm-4jk8kx's horizon on the strength of that argument rather than on the interoperability argument currently recorded.\n\n2. The consumer changes shape faster than the storage. Every token-efficiency decision in this portfolio - budgets (pm-5t33or), encodings (pm-kvxqp1), projections (pm-cxr0jb), packing (pm-4k6b) - is calibrated against the context windows and tokenizers of current coding agents. Those will change by orders of magnitude, in both directions, over the life of a decade-scale workspace: windows grow, but so does the number of agents sharing one budget. The durable form of this work is therefore not any particular budget number but the mechanism that lets budgets be re-derived: pm-t5dt4z (self-reported token accounting) and pm-8pnj (tokens per completed task as a CI-visible metric) are the two items that survive a tenfold change in consumer shape. Every hardcoded ceiling is a dated artifact. Recommend that the horizon policy classify budget numbers as explicitly dated and re-derivable, and classify the instruments that produce them as long-horizon.\n\n3. Immutability is a claim about the future, so it must be verifiable without us. w7ccmv makes history immutably recorded and independently verifiable. pm-3z0k (portable integrity attestation - export a detached proof bundle, verify it standalone) is what makes \"independently\" literally true: a third party with the bundle and no pm installation can confirm the record was not altered. On a decade scale that is the difference between a tamper-evidence claim and a tamper-evidence fact, because the party who needs to check will not be running this version of this tool. pm-3z0k currently sits at priority 3. Its priority is defensible on near-term value and understates its horizon value; recommend the horizon policy record that distinction rather than resolving it by re-prioritizing, since near-term sequencing should stay driven by near-term value.\n\nThe policy addition this note proposes, in one sentence: every portfolio item carries a horizon classification that is independent of its priority, where priority answers \"when should this be worked on\" and horizon answers \"how long will this decision bind\", and items whose horizon exceeds their priority - pm-4jk8kx, pm-3z0k, pm-e5yupa, pm-4020c5, and the format and vocabulary decisions generally - are flagged so that a cheap decision made today is not allowed to bind a workspace for twenty years without anyone noticing it was a twenty-year decision.\n\nWhy no seventh outcome milestone. The three forces above do not describe a new outcome; they describe durability constraints on outcomes that already exist. A \"decade-scale durability\" milestone would overlap w7ccmv and t4d7nz and would dilute a ladder whose current strength is that every rung is falsifiable. The correct home is this policy item and the horizon field it governs."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-22T18:24:13.924Z",codex-root,"Long-range planning stays useful when horizons are promotion states backed by evidence, not promised dates. Canonical work items remain the source of execution truth; the portfolio decision supplies only sequencing and promotion semantics."
tests[3]{command,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  pm dedupe-audit --mode parent_scope --json,project,240
  pm graph audit --json,project,240
  pm validate --check-resolution --check-history-drift --json,project,240
